%I A398677 #9 Aug 12 2026 10:44:58
%S A398677 101,131,173,191,236,281,446,461,551,641,701,731,761,821,866,911,971,
%T A398677 1031,1181,1361,1433,1451,1511,1559,1601,1706,1721,1811,1901,2021,
%U A398677 2081,2126,2231,2351,2441,2531,2693,2801,2846,2861,3011,3071,3176,3251,3281,3341,3386,3431,3491
%N A398677 Numbers k such that sigma(4*k+1) > sigma(4*k), where sigma(k) is the sum of divisors of k (A000203).
%C A398677 Numbers k such that A112610(k) > A193553(k).
%C A398677 The asymptotic density of this sequence exists and is in the interval [0.0107553, 0.0207187] (Luo and Ren, 2023).
%C A398677 The numbers of terms that do not exceed 10^k, for k = 3, 4, ..., are 17, 133, 1402, 13959, 138993, 1391892, 13926625, ... . It appears that the asymptotic density of this sequence equals 0.0139... .
%H A398677 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A398677/b398677.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398677 Xin-qi Luo and Chen-kai Ren, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.00295">On the natural density of integers n for which sigma(kn + r_1) > sigma(kn + r_2)</a>, arXiv:2311.00295 [math.NT], 2023-2026.
%e A398677 101 is a term since sigma(4*101+1) = 726 > sigma(4*101) = 714.
%t A398677 q[k_] := DivisorSigma[1, 4*k + 1] > DivisorSigma[1, 4*k]; Select[Range[3500], q]
%o A398677 (PARI) isok(k) = sigma(4*k+1) > sigma(4*k);
%Y A398677 Cf. A000203, A082957, A193553, A112610, A325423, A398676.
%K A398677 nonn,easy,new
